{"id":"e10t3","name":"March Sales per Product, Unsold Products Included","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The merchandising team wants a sales report for March 2024 that lists every product of the catalog, including the products that sold nothing, so that they can spot dead stock.</p>\n<h3>Tables</h3>\n<p><code>products</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>product_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(50)</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>category</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(30)</td>\n<td>may be NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>discontinued_on</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n<td>NULL if the product is still sold</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>orders</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>order_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>order_date</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>status</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(20)</td>\n<td><code>'completed'</code>, <code>'pending'</code>, <code>'cancelled'</code> or <code>'refunded'</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>order_items</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>order_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null, exists in <code>orders</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null, exists in <code>products</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>quantity</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null, strictly positive</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>unit_price</td>\n<td>DECIMAL(10,2)</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>An order can contain several lines for the same product.</p>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The report contains every product, except the products discontinued before <code>2024-03-01</code> (<code>discontinued_on &lt; '2024-03-01'</code>). A product with a NULL <code>discontinued_on</code>, or discontinued on or after <code>2024-03-01</code>, is included.</li>\n<li>An order line counts only if its order has status <code>'completed'</code> and an <code>order_date</code> between <code>2024-03-01</code> and <code>2024-03-31</code>, both inclusive.</li>\n<li><code>orders_count</code> is the number of distinct counted orders that contain the product, <code>units_sold</code> is the sum of <code>quantity</code>, and <code>revenue</code> is the sum of <code>quantity * unit_price</code> over the counted lines. A product without any counted line has <code>0</code>, <code>0</code> and <code>0.00</code>.</li>\n<li>A NULL <code>category</code> is reported as <code>'Uncategorized'</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>Exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>category</td>\n<td>VARCHAR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>product_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>orders_count</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>units_sold</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>revenue</td>\n<td>DECIMAL, 2 decimals</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>category</code> ascending, then <code>revenue</code> descending, then <code>product_id</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>products</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>product_id</th>\n<th>product_name</th>\n<th>category</th>\n<th>discontinued_on</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Pen</td>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Notebook</td>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Stapler</td>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>2024-02-15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Mouse</td>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>2024-03-20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Cable</td>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Mug</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>orders</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>order_id</th>\n<th>order_date</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>2024-03-02</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>2024-03-15</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>102</td>\n<td>2024-03-20</td>\n<td>cancelled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>103</td>\n<td>2024-02-28</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>2024-03-31</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>order_items</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>order_id</th>\n<th>product_id</th>\n<th>quantity</th>\n<th>unit_price</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>1.50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>25.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>1.50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>4.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>102</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>9.99</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>103</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>4.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>24.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>12.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>category</th>\n<th>product_id</th>\n<th>product_name</th>\n<th>orders_count</th>\n<th>units_sold</th>\n<th>revenue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Mouse</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>73.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Electronics</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Cable</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Pen</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>22.50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Office</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Notebook</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>8.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uncategorized</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Mug</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Dialect: PostgreSQL.</li>\n<li>Write a single <code>SELECT</code> statement (CTEs allowed). Do not create tables or views.</li>\n<li><code>products</code> has up to 10^5 rows, <code>orders</code> up to 10^6 rows, <code>order_items</code> up to 5 * 10^6 rows.</li>\n</ul><p class=\"muted\">Write a PostgreSQL query.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>products</code>, <code>orders</code>, <code>order_items</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>category</code>, <code>product_id</code>, <code>product_name</code>, <code>orders_count</code>, <code>units_sold</code>, <code>revenue</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°2, question 3","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>products</code>, <code>orders</code>, <code>order_items</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>category</code>, <code>product_id</code>, <code>product_name</code>, <code>orders_count</code>, <code>units_sold</code>, <code>revenue</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : ton test visible tourne.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 1/1. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 4 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"products":{"columns":[["product_id","INT"],["product_name","VARCHAR(50)"],["category","VARCHAR(30)"],["discontinued_on","DATE"]],"rows":[[1,"Pen","Office",null],[2,"Notebook","Office",null],[3,"Stapler","Office","2024-02-15"],[4,"Mouse","Electronics","2024-03-20"],[5,"Cable","Electronics",null],[6,"Mug",null,null]]},"orders":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["order_date","DATE"],["status","VARCHAR(20)"]],"rows":[[100,"2024-03-02","completed"],[101,"2024-03-15","completed"],[102,"2024-03-20","cancelled"],[103,"2024-02-28","completed"],[104,"2024-03-31","completed"]]},"order_items":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["product_id","INT"],["quantity","INT"],["unit_price","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[100,1,10,"1.50"],[100,4,1,"25.00"],[101,1,5,"1.50"],[101,2,2,"4.00"],[102,5,3,"9.99"],[103,2,7,"4.00"],[104,4,2,"24.00"],[104,3,4,"12.00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["category","product_id","product_name","orders_count","units_sold","revenue"],"rows":[["Electronics",4,"Mouse",2,3,73.0],["Electronics",5,"Cable",0,0,0.0],["Office",1,"Pen",2,15,22.5],["Office",2,"Notebook",1,2,8.0],["Uncategorized",6,"Mug",0,0,0.0]]}}],"hidden_n":4,"hidden":"","solution":""}